from common import *
src('igeeks-v3'); dom('mongodb')
topic('CRUD')
M('b','k',"What kind of database is MongoDB?","A document database that stores JSON-like (BSON) documents","A relational database with tables and joins only","A key-value store only","A graph database","Documents with flexible fields are grouped in collections.")
M('b','k',"What is a collection in MongoDB?","A group of documents, roughly like a table","A single document","A database server","An index","A collection holds documents that usually share a purpose but need not share a schema.")
M('b','k',"Which method inserts a single document?","insertOne()","add()","save() only","push()","db.users.insertOne({ name: 'Asha' }) adds one document and returns its _id.")
M('b','k',"Which method finds documents matching a filter?","find()","select()","get()","query()","db.users.find({ age: { $gt: 18 } }) returns a cursor over matching documents.")
M('b','k',"What is the _id field?","The unique primary key of every document, added automatically if missing","An optional label","A reference to another collection","The document size","MongoDB creates an ObjectId by default. The _id index is unique.")
M('b','k',"Which update operator changes the value of a field?","$set","$put","$change","$assign","db.users.updateOne({ _id: id }, { $set: { age: 30 } }) changes only the named field.")
M('b','k',"Which method deletes all documents matching a filter?","deleteMany()","removeAll()","dropMany()","clear()","deleteOne removes the first match and deleteMany removes every match.")
M('b','k',"Which operator means greater than in a query filter?","$gt","$greater","$more","$above","$gt, $gte, $lt, $lte, $eq and $ne are the comparison operators.")
M('b','k',"Which format does MongoDB use to store documents internally?","BSON","XML","CSV","YAML","BSON is a binary JSON-like format with extra types such as Date and ObjectId.")
M('b','k',"Which method sorts the results of a query?","sort({ field: 1 })","order()","arrange()","orderBy()","1 means ascending and -1 means descending.")
M('b','k',"What does db.users.find({}).limit(5) return?","At most five documents","Exactly five documents","The first five fields","The count of documents","limit caps the number of documents the cursor returns.")
M('b','k',"What does db.users.countDocuments({ active: true }) return?","The number of documents that match the filter","The size of the collection in bytes","The list of matching documents","The number of indexes","countDocuments runs a count with the filter. estimatedDocumentCount uses metadata and takes no filter.")
topic('Schema Design')
M('b','k',"Which feature lets documents in one collection have different fields?","Flexible schema","Normalisation","Foreign keys","Stored procedures","MongoDB does not force a fixed schema, although validation rules can be added.")
M('b','k',"What is an ObjectId?","A 12-byte unique identifier used by default for _id","A password hash","An index name","A collection name","It contains a timestamp, random value and counter, so ids are roughly time-ordered.")
M('b','k',"Which tool is the official graphical interface for MongoDB?","MongoDB Compass","phpMyAdmin","pgAdmin","SQL Developer","Compass lets you browse data, build queries and analyse indexes.")
M('b','k',"Which cloud service hosts MongoDB as a managed database?","MongoDB Atlas","Firebase","DynamoDB","Redis Cloud","Atlas runs MongoDB clusters on cloud providers with backups and monitoring.")
topic('Aggregation')
M('i','k',"What is the aggregation pipeline?","A sequence of stages that transform documents, such as $match then $group","A way to copy a collection","A list of indexes","A replication method","Each stage passes its output to the next.")
M('i','k',"Which aggregation stage groups documents and computes totals such as sums?","$group","$project","$sort","$limit","$group uses an _id expression for the key and accumulators such as $sum and $avg.")
M('i','k',"Why place $match as early as possible in a pipeline?","It reduces the number of documents later stages must process and can use indexes","It sorts the data","It is required first by syntax","It adds an index","An early $match filters data before heavier stages.")
topic('CRUD')
M('i','k',"What does the upsert option do in an update?","Inserts a new document if no document matches the filter","Updates every document","Deletes unmatched documents","Creates an index","updateOne(filter, update, { upsert: true }) either updates the match or creates a document from the filter and update.")
M('i','k',"Which operator adds an item to an array field?","$push","$add","$append","$insert","$push appends a value. $addToSet adds only when the value is not already present.")
M('i','k',"What does { age: { $in: [20, 30] } } match?","Documents whose age is 20 or 30","Documents whose age is between 20 and 30","Documents with an array age","Documents without age","$in matches any value in the list.")
topic('Indexing & Performance')
M('i','k',"What does an index on a field do?","Speeds up queries on that field at the cost of extra storage and slower writes","Encrypts the field","Makes the field unique automatically","Removes duplicates","Without an index MongoDB scans the whole collection (a COLLSCAN).")
M('i','k',"What does explain() show for a query?","How MongoDB plans to run it, including whether an index is used","The contents of the result","The server logs","The user permissions","Look for IXSCAN (index used) versus COLLSCAN (full scan) and compare documents examined with documents returned.")
topic('Schema Design')
M('i','k',"When is embedding related data in one document usually a good choice?","When the data is read together and the embedded part is small and bounded","When the embedded data grows without limit","When many documents must share it","When it changes constantly on its own","Embedding gives single-read access. Unbounded arrays risk the 16 MB document limit.")
topic('Aggregation')
M('a','k',"What does $lookup do in an aggregation pipeline?","Performs a left outer join with another collection","Searches text","Looks up an index","Converts types","$lookup adds an array of matching documents from the foreign collection to each input document.")
M('a','k',"What does $unwind do?","Outputs one document for each element of an array field","Removes a field","Sorts an array","Flattens a nested object","A document with a three-element array becomes three documents, each with one element.")
topic('Indexing & Performance')
M('a','k',"A compound index is on { a: 1, b: 1 }. Which query can use it efficiently for its filter?","{ a: 5, b: 6 }, and also { a: 5 }","{ b: 6 } only","Neither a nor b queries","Only { b: 6, a: 5 } when written in that order","An index can serve queries on a left prefix of its keys (a, or a and b). A query on b alone cannot use the index for seeking.")
M('a','k',"What is a covered query?","A query answered entirely from an index without reading documents","A query that is encrypted","A query inside a transaction","A query on a capped collection","It needs all filtered and returned fields to be in the index and _id excluded unless indexed.")
M('a','k',"What does a TTL index do?","Automatically removes documents after a set time","Encrypts documents with a key","Limits write speed","Duplicates documents to another server","TTL indexes work on date fields and are useful for sessions and logs.")
topic('Replication & Sharding')
M('a','k',"What is a replica set?","A group of mongod instances holding the same data, with one primary and secondaries","A set of shard keys","A backup file","A cluster of query routers","Replication provides redundancy and automatic failover through elections.")
M('a','k',"In a replica set, which member accepts writes by default?","The primary","Any secondary","The arbiter","The config server","Secondaries replicate from the primary. Reads from secondaries may be stale.")
M('a','k',"What does sharding do?","Spreads a large collection across several servers by a shard key","Copies data for backup","Compresses data","Encrypts data","A poor shard key (for example a monotonically increasing value) can create a hot shard.")
topic('Transactions & Consistency')
M('a','k',"What does write concern { w: 'majority' } mean?","The write is acknowledged only after a majority of replica set members have it","The write goes to a majority of collections","The write is cached","The write is faster","It protects against losing a write after a failover, at the cost of latency.")
M('a','k',"When are multi-document transactions most appropriate in MongoDB?","When several documents must change atomically and a schema redesign cannot avoid it","For every single insert","Instead of indexes","Only on standalone servers","Single-document operations are already atomic, and good schema design often removes the need for transactions.")
topic('Schema Design')
M('a','k',"What is the main risk of an array in a document that can grow without bound?","The document may exceed the 16 MB size limit and updates become slower","Arrays cannot be indexed","Arrays are not allowed in BSON","It disables the _id index","Use a separate collection with references, or bucket documents, for unbounded data.")
M('a','k',"What does the $set operator on a nested path such as { 'address.city': 'Pune' } do?","Updates only the city field inside the address subdocument","Replaces the whole address object","Creates a new collection","Fails because of the dot","Dot notation targets a field inside an embedded document without replacing the rest of it.")
